[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent and controlled source requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-DC
TITLE: DC voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a dc voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and a signed constant and explicit polarity. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare operating point and a two-point DC sweep.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-AC
TITLE: AC voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a ac voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and magnitude and phase in degrees, plus an independently editable DC bias. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare real and imaginary AC response at zero and ninety degrees.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-PULSE
TITLE: Pulse voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a pulse voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and low/high levels, delay, rise, fall, width and period. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check both edges, both steady levels and repetition over two periods.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-SIN
TITLE: Sinusoidal voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a sinusoidal voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and offset, amplitude, frequency, delay, phase and damping. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check pre-delay value, first period, and damped envelope.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-PWL
TITLE: Piecewise linear voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a piecewise linear voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and ordered time/value pairs and explicit repetition policy. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check breakpoints, interpolation, duplicate times and invalid ordering.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-PWLFILE
TITLE: File-backed piecewise linear voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a file-backed piecewise linear voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and a bounded waveform asset with explicit time and value units. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare samples with the inline equivalent, then refuse malformed and unavailable assets.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-EXP
TITLE: Exponential voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a exponential voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and initial and pulsed levels, independent delays and time constants. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check both exponential segments at their time constants.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-SFFM
TITLE: Frequency modulated voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a frequency modulated voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and offset, amplitude, carrier frequency, modulation index and signal frequency. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare the waveform and its carrier sidebands.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-AM
TITLE: Amplitude modulated voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a amplitude modulated voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and offset, carrier and modulation frequencies, amplitude and delay. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare carrier, envelope and delayed startup.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-PAT
TITLE: Pattern voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a pattern voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and low/high levels, bit sequence, timing and repeat rules. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check sequence ordering, transition times and repeat termination.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-NOISE
TITLE: Transient noise voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a transient noise voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and amplitude, sampling interval and a replay seed when the selected profile supports it. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check replay and statistical bounds under a pinned sample count.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-V-RANDOM
TITLE: Transient random voltage source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a transient random voltage source with ordered positive and negative terminals and distribution, distribution parameters, hold interval and replay seed. Values shall use volts and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Check the held value between draws, replay, and distribution limits.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SRC-C-DC
TITLE: DC current source
STATEMENT: >>>
The catalog shall provide a dc current source with ordered positive and negative terminals and a signed constant and explicit polarity. Values shall use amperes and waveform time shall use seconds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Catalog target. Compare operating point and a two-point DC sweep.
<<<

